Replaces the author-written survey with an assessment in which every item is
reproduced from, or documented as an adaptation of, a published instrument.

New:
- lib/instruments.js  — full item bank with per-item provenance (verbatim /
  adapted / contextual), source citations, reported psychometrics and licensing.
  MAAS-15 and the CFPB 10-item scale verbatim; Big Three + Big Five verbatim;
  bias subscales adapted from Ritika & Kishor (2022) and Costa et al. (2025);
  financial FOMO adapted from Przybylski et al. (2013); a newly developed
  Social Media Financial Influence scale built from Ni et al. (2020) and
  Ohanian (1990).
- lib/scoring.js      — construct scoring with the two rules applied papers get
  wrong: MAAS is not reverse-coded, and CFPB is an IRT lookup rather than a
  linear sum (raw total always returned; lookup table left as a documented gap).
  POMP normalisation for the composite bias index. Careless-responding flags.
- lib/scenarios.js    — Simulated Social Media Feed with four randomised arms
  (control / disclosure / prebunk / mindful pause) and a within-participant
  social-proof manipulation. All posts fictional.
- lib/flow.js         — 16-screen journey: welcome, about, consent, eligibility,
  profile, use, influence, four bias blocks, feed, MAAS, CFPB, literacy, results.
- lib/learn.js        — micro-modules and weekly challenges per construct.
- components/Assessment.jsx, FeedSim.jsx, Results.jsx
- server/responses.js — item-level storage, aggregate view, key-gated CSV export
  in wide and long (per-trial) formats.

Deprecated: lib/survey.js and components/Survey.jsx retained for interpreting
v1.0 data only; no longer reachable from the UI.

