+    what: "Overprecision is being too sure of a specific number or outcome — and it grows with the volume of information you consume, even when the extra information adds nothing.",
+    why: "More content raises confidence much faster than it raises accuracy. This is why an hour of scrolling can leave you feeling certain and no better informed.",
