From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 04:41:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Unify into a single app: landing -> assessment -> hub

Removes the parallel "assessment" and "tools" experiences. There is now one
route through the product.

- App.jsx reduced to a three-stage shell (landing / assess / hub). Completion
  is remembered, so returning visitors land in the hub.
- New Hub.jsx: the single post-assessment home, with one navigation covering
  results, learning, challenge, spending tracking, live feed and community.
  All exploratory-tool state moved here out of App.jsx.
- New LearnPanel.jsx: the Improve phase promoted to a first-class section,
  with modules ordered by the participant's own construct scores, per-module
  completion tracking and a progress bar.
- Results.jsx gains `embedded` (drops its duplicate Learn tab inside the hub)
  and `onContinue` (hands off to the dashboard at the end of the assessment).
  Submission state now persists, so a reload cannot double-submit.
- Landing rewritten around a single primary action, with a Continue route for
  participants who have already completed the assessment.
- Sections that depend on assessment answers gate on completion rather than
  rendering an empty dashboard.

