From 62358ff67e8d460d1373dbf6bf99e70ccea6c617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 10:34:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Close remaining spec gaps: check-up, block bars, quiz
 feedback, HTML report
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Screen 16 — Monthly check-up (was missing entirely):
- lib/history.js records each completed assessment as a wave summary and
  compares the two most recent, direction-aware: a fall in bias and a rise in
  mindfulness both count as improvement.
- components/CheckUp.jsx renders three states — no assessment, one wave
  (baseline + "come back in N days"), and a full comparison with per-metric
  and per-bias deltas plus a wave log. Added as a hub section.
- A 28-day minimum interval is recommended in the interface, since re-taking
  sooner mostly measures recall of previous answers rather than change.

Screen 13 — Results dashboard now uses segmented block bars (███████░░░) with
High / Moderate / Low badges, matching the specified profile format.

Screen 12 — Financial literacy quiz is now interactive: immediate correct or
incorrect marking, the right answer revealed, and a plain-language explanation
per item. "Do not know" is acknowledged rather than marked wrong, so the
option stays psychologically free to choose.

Screen 1 — Welcome gains the specified "Learn more" action.

Screen 9 — Feed decisions reworded to the specified Yes / need more
information / No, with "Would you invest?" and "Why?" as the prompts.

Screen 10 — Item randomisation added, seeded from the participant code so the
order is stable across a refresh, applied to the SMFI scale and the adapted
bias subscales. The MAAS is deliberately excluded: it is normed in its
published order and its reported reliability applies to that order. The order
actually presented is stored with the response so order effects can be tested.

Personalised report is now a styled, self-contained HTML document with a
print-to-PDF action, covering influence, bias profile, mindfulness, well-being,
practical tips and the weekly challenge, replacing the plain-text version.

Also fixes a CSS collision: the check-up trend bars shared a class name with
the pre-existing score mini-chart and rendered as empty boxes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J99CXD5HFH9Tpa7mP78gNy
