From bc2c6a1a7e605973110fdea148783f8fbe6d5182 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:31:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Add a PowerShell walkthrough for Windows deployment
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DEPLOY.md assumes a Unix-style shell. This adds a Windows equivalent with
every command written as copy-paste PowerShell, covering the platform-specific
problems that actually stop people:

- npm.ps1 blocked by the default execution policy, which is the most common
  first error on a fresh Windows setup
- PowerShell aliasing `curl` to Invoke-WebRequest, which behaves differently —
  the checks use Invoke-RestMethod / Invoke-WebRequest instead
- Copy-Item nesting client\client when you copy the folder rather than its
  contents
- PATH not refreshing until PowerShell is reopened after installing Node

Two routes are given: git am for people who have Git, and an Expand-Archive
plus Copy-Item route for those who do not, with a timestamped backup taken
before anything is overwritten. Also includes a reusable get-data.ps1 that
downloads both CSV exports to dated files and prints the row counts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J99CXD5HFH9Tpa7mP78gNy
---
 DEPLOY-POWERSHELL.md | 361 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 DEPLOY.md            |   4 +
 2 files changed, 365 insertions(+)
